[-] baron		<-->	noun++C1	[221031][002]	./ˈbærən/-NAmE /ˈbærən/ [t]
	;chúa đất -- (1) a nobleman of the lowest rank. In the UK, barons use the title Lord; in other countries they use the title Baron.
			;Topics HISTORy-C1, People in societyc1
	; -- (2) a person who owns or controls a large part of a particular industry
		;a press baron
		;the oil barons of Texas
		;see also drug baron
				;Oxford Collocations Dictionary
				;adjective
				;medianewspaperpress…
